{
  "description": "What a write that reads alike a recorded one is to that record (#275), written by hand. The dispatch fingerprint is published, persisted and re-derived when a book is read, and it digests the request as ParseJSON reads it, so two different writes can share one: a float64 holds 9007199254740993 and 9007199254740992 as one number. The published fingerprint does not change; the decision is made from the exact text every row records. cases: same is answered from the record and not run; different runs and makes its own record; conflict is refused with DurableRequestConflict, neither run nor answered. Each pair has one fingerprint. recordable: whether the durable record can hold a call's text as written; one it cannot is refused with DurableRequestUnrecordable before anything is claimed, unless a row a published release wrote answers it first. resume: each call, in order, on a run resumed from contract/testdata/durable-writes/published-checkpoints.json, and what it gets: its record, a run, a refusal, or HostOutcomeUnknown. items are dispatch rows as they are written. compareDurableRequests in go/context/run_writer.go and packages/harness/storage/writer.ts read every case, and tests/test_contract.py derives each decision from its text.",
